10:22] Evan**: Fair question — I should have looked harder before wiring it in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:54] Charlie**: Following up on this — since the replacement turned out to be AGPL, I'm searching for an Apache or MIT alternative that can do the same parsing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:56] Diana**: Any candidates yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 09:58] Charlie**: A couple, but neither one covers everything the old library did. Still unresolved as of today — going to keep looking rather than force a bad fit.\\n\\n**[2026-08-15 10:22] Alice**: Let me know as soon as one of those candidates looks viable — don't want this dragging past the rest of the release work.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 41 slack thread licens parser swap channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 11 last activ 2026 08 15 2026 08 11 10 16 evan finish the parser swap the audit flag pull out the problem librari and drop in a replac call that step done 2026 08 11 1018 diana nice turnaround i ll fold it into the re scan 2026 08 11 10 21 charli did you check the new one s licens close or just take the packag list at face valu 2026 08 11 10 22 evan fair question i should have look harder befor wire it in 2026 08 15 09 54 charli follow up on this sinc the replac turn out to be agpl i m search for an apach or mit altern that can do the same pars 2026 08 15 09 56 diana ani candid yet 2026 08 15 09 58 charli a coupl but neither one cover everyth the old librari did still unresolv a of today go to keep look rather than forc a bad fit 2026 08 15 10 22 alic let me know a soon a one of those candid look viabl don t want this drag past the rest of the releas work\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede7c6ba8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"id\": \"42a19cccc47f5107\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35174469663645447, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15363729519493496, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8139953, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede7c6ba8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-11-license-parser-swap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1186, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:39\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-39\\n\\n# Slack Thread: License Audit\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 11:13] Diana**: Starting the third-party license audit across the dependency tree — need a full inventory before we sign off on anything for release.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:37] Alice**: Watch closely for GPL or AGPL. Our client agreements rule out shipping copyleft code in the core engine.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 12:46] Diana**: That's exactly what I'm scanning for, using license-checker against the dependency manifests to flag anything outside MIT/Apache/BSD.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:19] Bob**: Are you following transitive dependencies too? A clean top-level library can still pull in something restrictive underneath.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:24] Diana**: Yes, doing a recursive pass, not just the direct dependencies.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 13:51] Evan**: Want a hand with the Docker base image layers once the app-level scan is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 14:07] Diana**: That'd help. Still working through the results — nothing conclusive to report yet, I'll have the full inventory soon.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 39 slack thread licens audit channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 09 2026 08 09 11 13 diana start the third parti licens audit across the depend tree need a full inventori befor we sign off on anyth for releas 2026 08 09 12 37 alic watch close for gpl or agpl our client agreement rule out ship copyleft code in the core engin 2026 08 09 12 46 diana that s exact what i m scan for use licens checker against the depend manifest to flag anyth outsid mit apach bsd 2026 08 09 13 19 bob are you follow transit depend too a clean top level librari can still pull in someth restrict underneath 2026 08 09 13 24 diana yes do a recurs pas not just the direct depend 2026 08 09 13 51 evan want a hand with the docker base imag layer onc the app level scan is done 2026 08 09 14 07 diana that d help still work through the result noth conclus to report yet i ll have the full inventori soon\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0111388a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"id\": \"55d2a5f5995c8f55\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32046550204667923, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11768067435239896, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7936301, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0111388a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-license-audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1085, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:15\", \"token_count\": 310, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-05\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offset Mismatch Debugging\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 08:56] Charlie**: @Diana, I'm seeing weird behavior in the test cases. The redaction masks are shifted by a character or two in some PDF exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:01] Diana**: Multi-column layouts? I told you pdfminer output was injecting spaces.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:43] Charlie**: It's not just the spaces. The engine sees the text at one offset, but the PDF coordinates are different after the cleaning phase.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:51] Diana**: Are you seeing this on all viewers? Sometimes Acrobat renders overlays differently than Chrome's PDF viewer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:52] Charlie**: Looking at the raw coordinate output for now. Whitespace normalization looks like the culprit — non-breaking spaces keep showing up in the extracted text.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:53] Charlie**: Still stuck. Tried mapping cleaned offsets back to raw ones, but the math falls apart on dense pages.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:40] Diana**: Can we get most of the standard text aligned and park the edge cases?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:42] Charlie**: Not really — on dense docs it's closer to half the spans. Starting to look like an upstream pdfminer.six issue. I'm going to check their tracker.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:45] Alice**: Status?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:47] Charlie**: No. Offline tonight.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 05 slack thread offset mismatch debug channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 23 2026 06 23 08 56 charli diana i m see weird behavior in the test case the redact mask are shift by a charact or two in some pdf export 2026 06 23 09 01 diana multi column layout i told you pdfminer output wa inject space 2026 06 23 09 43 charli it s not just the space the engin see the text at one offset but the pdf coordin are differ after the clean phase 2026 06 23 10 51 diana are you see this on all viewer sometim acrobat render overlay differ than chrome s pdf viewer 2026 06 23 10 52 charli look at the raw coordin output for now whitespac normal look like the culprit non break space keep show up in the extract text 2026 06 23 10 53 charli still stuck tri map clean offset back to raw one but the math fall apart on dens page 2026 06 23 12 40 diana can we get most of the standard text align and park the edg case 2026 06 23 12 42 charli not realli on dens doc it s closer to half the span start to look like an upstream pdfminer six issu i m go to check their tracker 2026 06 23 12 45 alic status 2026 06 23 12 47 charli no offlin tonight\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee2707448a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"id\": \"30c128c9ab691c29\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.312989548183391, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1262236259762728, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7487767, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee2707448a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1387, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:41\", \"token_count\": 405, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie opened on the AGPL PDF-parser problem and the search for an Apache/MIT alternative. Evan noted the earlier Windows path fix; code-signing cert procurement remains open.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: Licensing first — the replacement PDF parser Evan swapped in turned out to be AGPL. I've started searching for an Apache or MIT alternative. Need to confirm feature coverage before we swap again.\\n\\n**Diana**: Right — AGPL isn't acceptable for how we're distributing the toolkit.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Unknown how much rework another swap costs until I compare candidates. That's this week's task. I'd rather not guess.\\n\\n**Evan**: Separate note while we're all here — the Windows backslash path handling fix from earlier this month has been holding up fine in the build. No regressions there.\\n\\n**Alice**: Good to hear. And signing?\\n\\n**Evan**: Still waiting on the code-signing certificate to come through procurement. No firm timeline yet, so I can't say when that's cleared.\\n\\n**Alice**: Okay — Charlie, keep pushing on the parser alternative, that's the priority. Evan, keep chasing procurement on the cert, but no need for a deep-dive there today.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli open on the agpl pdf parser problem and the search for an apach mit altern evan note the earlier window path fix code sign cert procur remain open sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli licens first the replac pdf parser evan swap in turn out to be agpl i ve start search for an apach or mit altern need to confirm featur coverag befor we swap again dia